\p{The one unit of this class in these corpora, \code{Std.IterM.Equiv.lift_step_bind_congr}, is a verdict of the machine now, equal to the reference engine's, and the 21,926 ticks that Std gained are its second run. An earlier build failed the memo audit of this gate on the same unit (the trigger fired inside the audit's re-computation of a judgment that the run itself had answered by a shortcut); the trigger is skipped inside an audit since then.}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.4 The eight corpora: declines before and after, and the differential engine}

\p{The executable, 8 workers. "Declined" counts decline events of the machine: every declined unit is tried twice (the driver's cold retry). Before: the published build with the machine's decline log (section 1). After: the final build under the differential engine (\code{\verb~|-X engine=diff~}: the reference engine checks every unit beside the machine, and a unit on which the two differ is a disagreement).}

\table{
\tr{\th{Corpus}\th{Declined before}\th{of them this rule}\th{Declined after}\th{of them this rule}\th{Runs in exact-let mode}\th{K comparisons through a let variable with two types}\th{of them with different answers}\th{Reference engine: units, accepted}\th{Disagreements}}
\tr{\td{Init}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{57,938; 57,938}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{Std}\td{2}\td{2}\td{0}\td{0}\td{1}\td{0}\td{0}\td{100,096; 100,096}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{cedar}\td{2}\td{2}\td{0}\td{0}\td{1}\td{0}\td{0}\td{144,098; 144,098}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{reachability}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{0}\td{4,224; 4,224}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{con-leche}\td{4}\td{2}\td{2}\td{0}\td{1}\td{0}\td{0}\td{36,274; 36,274}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{navier-stokes-euler}\td{32}\td{32}\td{0}\td{0}\td{17}\td{0}\td{0}\td{124,850; 124,850}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{cslib}\td{22}\td{14}\td{10}\td{\strong{2}}\td{8}\td{3}\td{0}\td{397,608; 397,608}\td{0}}
\tr{\td{Mathlib}\td{128}\td{120}\td{18}\td{\strong{10}}\td{65}\td{10}\td{0}\td{714,712; 714,712}\td{0}}
}

\p{\strong{80 of the 86 units of the class are verdicts of the machine}, all accepts, each equal to the reference engine's. \strong{Six stay declines}, all by the rule for an over-application (4.4): \code{Cslib.Query.IsSort.lowerBound_infinite} of cslib, and of Mathlib \code{AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isCoverDense_toOver_Spec}, \code{AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.isOneHypercoverDense_toOver_Spec}, \code{MeasureTheory.integral_eq_of_hasDerivAt_off_countable_of_le}, \code{ModularGroup.tendsto_lcRow0} and \code{MvQPF.liftR_map_last}. The other declines after the patch are eager reduction (one unit of con-leche, four of cslib, four of Mathlib), another package's class. The mode ran 93 units: the 86 and 7 more that the wider triggers of 4.5 start (navier-stokes-euler 1, cslib 1, Mathlib 5), which the base decided by a reading that is the official one only inside the scope; all seven are accepted in the mode.}

\p{\strong{Accept runs}: the eight corpora with 8 and with 4 workers through the executable and through the JVM launcher, no option: 32 runs, 32 accepts, no warm anomaly, no machine-incomplete unit, no disagreement; decline events per run 0, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 10, 18 in the order of the table, in every one of the four configurations; the largest resident set 4,539 MiB (Mathlib, JVM launcher, 8 workers).}

\p{\strong{Every declaration in exact-let mode against the reference engine} (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.letexact=always -X machine.switches=none -X engine=diff~}, 8 workers, the executable): 8 runs, 8 accepts, no disagreement on any unit. The mode ran 1,443,334 times, kept 172,023 applications and made 79 K comparisons through a let variable with two types, none with different answers. It ended 14 times without a verdict (cslib 2, Mathlib 12; every unit is tried twice), each time by the rule for an over-application. The other 19,238 decline events of these runs are eager reduction.}
}

\subtree{
\title{8.5 Counters: what changes and what does not}

\p{One worker in file order, the executable, the statistics file and the unit trace (steps and outcome of every checked unit), the eight corpora, three lanes: the base; the final build; the final build with the rule of 2026-11-24 switched back on (\code{\verb~|-Drlvm.machine.letexact=off -Drlvm.machine.letwide=false -Drlvm.machine.letroot=off~}).}

\ul{
\li{\strong{With the old rule on, the final build computes what the base computes}: on each of the eight corpora every count key of the machine, the reference engine, the driver and the loader is equal (the nine new \code{let.*} keys aside), and every unit has the same steps and the same outcome. So the first run of a declaration is what it was, and the new test in the loop of APPLY flags nothing on these corpora that the old tests did not flag.}
\li{\strong{With the new rule}, the outcome of a unit changes on 80 units, each from declined to accepted: Std 1, cedar 1, con-leche 1, navier-stokes-euler 16, cslib 6, Mathlib 55. The units the reference engine decides in such a run go from 1, 1, 2, 16, 11, 64 to 0, 0, 1, 0, 5, 9.}
\li{\strong{Not identical otherwise}, and this is the one place where the gate "only the units that were declined may change" does not hold to the letter: units checked by the same worker \em{after} the first unit of the class take other steps, with the same outcome: Std 2, cedar 84, con-leche 1, navier-stokes-euler 5,924, cslib 3,325, Mathlib 16,060 (none before the first unit of the class; about half of them fewer steps, half more; net -2,571 to +688,010 steps per corpus; the units that run a second time without changing their outcome are among them: the seven extra runs in the mode and the six units that are declined after it). The base's driver discards the worker's context after a decline, the patched unit is accepted and the context stays; from there on the resets of the warm session at its size cap fall on other units (Mathlib: 11,919 resets in the base, 11,900 with the patch), and a unit that starts in a session with another history takes other steps. The mechanism was followed as far as the count of resets, not further.}
\li{\strong{Ticks of the machine} (one worker): Init and reachability equal to the tick; Std +0.018 \%, cedar +0.010 \%, con-leche +0.062 \%, navier-stokes-euler +0.433 \%, cslib +0.030 \%, Mathlib +0.511 \% (559,746,444 to 562,608,349). The base's number leaves out what the reference engine did on the declined units.}
}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{9. The guard}

\p{The guard of [the decision on the default set](dec-YP0N): no corpus more than 3 \% slower than without the change, over at least three interleaved rounds. Warm wall clock of a pass that reloads the file with pipelined loading, 8 workers, the default configuration, the aarch64 development host. Every number was taken inside a quiet-core window (\src{bench/quiet.py}), all corpora of a launcher in one window, the variants interleaved round by round on each corpus. A cell is the mean over the three rounds of the median later pass of one process, in seconds; on reachability, whose pass is shorter than 0.5 s, the mean of the later passes. A process makes 15 passes on reachability, 10 on Init and Std, 8 on cedar, 6 on con-leche, cslib and navier-stokes-euler, 4 on Mathlib. After the cell: the three rounds, the CPU seconds of a pass, the loader's seconds, the peak resident set. \strong{Base}: a private build of the unpatched tree of 22:44 UTC, made with the same command as the candidate (jars \code{3babbe8de8f3}); its machine jar is byte for byte the published one, so on the launcher that runs the jars base and candidate differ in the jar of the machine and in nothing else. \strong{Candidate}: the final build. Every process accepted every unit.}

